second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What conflict is the Battle of Beirut associated with?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 117, \"text\": \"Battle of Beirut (1912) The Battle of Beirut was a naval battle off the coast of Beirut during the Italo-Turkish War.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d00\", \"start\": 118, \"end\": 321, \"text\": \"Italian fears that the Ottoman naval forces at Beirut could be used to threaten the approach to the Suez canal led the Italian military to order the destruction of the Ottoman naval presence in the area.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d00\", \"start\": 322, \"end\": 493, \"text\": \"On 24 February 1912 two Italian armoured cruisers attacked and sank an Ottoman casemate corvette and six lighters, retired, then returned and sank an Ottoman torpedo boat.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d00\", \"start\": 494, \"end\": 581, \"text\": \"As a result of the battle all Ottoman naval forces in the region were annihilated, thus\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 136, \"text\": \"Battle of Beirut (1941) The Battle of Beirut (12 July 1941) marked the end of hostilities in the Syria-Lebanon campaign of World War II.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d01\", \"start\": 137, \"end\": 576, \"text\": \"The campaign saw the initial Allied deployment of 2 brigades of the Australian 7th Division, a brigade from the 1st British Cavalry Division, the 5th Indian Infantry Brigade which was deployed immediately from Eritrea after the surrender of the Duke of Aosta, several armoured and air units of the British 6th Division, a special commando force (C battalion of the Special Service Brigade) and 6 battalions of the 1st Free French Division.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d01\", \"start\": 577, \"end\": 592, \"text\": \"On 8 July, even\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 24, \"text\": \"Casualties and losses c.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d02\", \"start\": 25, \"end\": 66, \"text\": \"4,652 Australian : 1,552 Free French : c.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d02\", \"start\": 67, \"end\": 87, \"text\": \"1,300 Jordanian : c.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d02\", \"start\": 88, \"end\": 563, \"text\": \"250 British and Indian : 1,800 , 1,200 POW , 3,150 sick 41 aircraft [ 2 ] Vichy France : 6,352 ( Vichy figures ) 8,912 ( British figures ) 179 aircraft 1 submarine sunk 5,668 defectors Germany : 4 aircraft [ 1 ] v t e Campaigns of World War II Europe Poland Polish resistance Phoney War Finland Winter War Karelia Lapland Denmark and Norway Western Front 1940 Resistance 1944–1945 Alps 1940 1944 Britain Balkans Serbian Partisans Greek resistance Eastern Front Chechnya Italy\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 708, \"text\": \"Klaus Barbie trial WW II theatres : Atlantic Western Front Eastern Front Mediterranean and Middle East Pacific Sino Japanese v t e World War II Outline Battles Operations Leaders Allied Axis Commanders Casualties Conferences General Topics Air warfare of World War II In Europe Blitzkrieg Comparative military ranks Cryptography Declarations of war Diplomacy Governments in exile Home front Australian United Kingdom United States Lend-Lease Manhattan Project British contribution Military awards Military equipment Military production Naval history Nazi plunder Opposition Technology Allied cooperation Mulberry harbour Total war Strategic bombing Puppet states Women Art and World War II Music in World War\"}, \"D5S1\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d04\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 59, \"text\": \"this would result in \\\"the excessive killings of civilians.\\\"\"}, \"D5S2\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d04\", \"start\": 60, \"end\": 171, \"text\": \"Following the siege of Beirut, Arafat fled to Greece, and then to Tunis, establishing a new headquarters there.\"}, \"D5S3\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d04\", \"start\": 172, \"end\": 307, \"text\": \"PLO \\\"fedayeen\\\" continued to operate out of Yemen, Jordan, Algeria, Iraq, and the Sudan, as well as within Israeli-controlled territory.\"}, \"D5S4\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d04\", \"start\": 308, \"end\": 426, \"text\": \"Decades after the siege, the event was cited by Osama bin Laden as a major reason for the September 11, 2001, attacks.\"}, \"D5S5\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d04\", \"start\": 427, \"end\": 593, \"text\": \"Siege of Beirut The Siege of Beirut took place in the summer of 1982, as part of the 1982 Lebanon War, which resulted from the breakdown of the cease-fire effected by\"}, \"D6S1\": {\"document_number\": 6, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d05\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 30, \"text\": \"in a single air attack alone .\"}, \"D6S2\": {\"document_number\": 6, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d05\", \"start\": 31, \"end\": 103, \"text\": \"Israeli long-range artillery targeted Syrian strongpoints to the north .\"}, \"D6S3\": {\"document_number\": 6, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d05\", \"start\": 104, \"end\": 298, \"text\": \"Israeli armored forces with artillery support attacked Syrian positions along the highway , with the objective of driving them from the highway all the way back to the edge of the Bekaa Valley .\"}, \"D6S4\": {\"document_number\": 6, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d05\", \"start\": 299, \"end\": 437, \"text\": \"[ 17 ] With air and artillery support mostly limited to targets north of the highway , the fighting was fierce , especially to the south .\"}, \"D6S5\": {\"document_number\": 6, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d05\", \"start\": 438, \"end\": 549, \"text\": \"By the end of the day , Israel accepted an American request for a cease-fire and halted its offensive , but the\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Battle of Beirut\", \"scope\": \"conflict\", \"claim\": \"The Battle of Beirut is associated with the Italo-Turkish War.\", \"answer\": \"Italo-Turkish War\", \"quote\": \"Battle of Beirut (1912) The Battle of Beirut was a naval battle off the coast of Beirut during the Italo-Turkish War.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Battle of Beirut\", \"scope\": \"conflict\", \"claim\": \"The Battle of Beirut is associated with World War II.\", \"answer\": \"World War II\", \"quote\": \"Battle of Beirut (1941) The Battle of Beirut (12 July 1941) marked the end of hostilities in the Syria-Lebanon campaign of World War II.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d04\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0348-d384050a4c81:d04:c0\", \"entity\": \"Battle of Beirut\", \"scope\": \"conflict\", \"claim\": \"The Battle of Beirut is associated with the 1982 Lebanon War.\", \"answer\": \"1982 Lebanon War\", \"quote\": \"Siege of Beirut The Siege of Beirut took place in the summer of 1982, as part of the